Start ready on iOS without SDL_main.

SDL_main.h makes iOS require SDL's own main()/SDL_RunApp, which calls
SDL_SetMainReady(). Here SDL is a library loaded into a running app, and
Minecraft never calls SDL_SetMainReady(), so SDL_Init failed with "Application
didn't initialize properly". The UIKit driver needs neither SDL's main nor
its app delegate, so SDL starts ready, and its main thread is the first thread
that calls into it (no debug assertion between main and video thread).

diff --git a/src/SDL.c b/src/SDL.c
index 3e61b8a..b41a261 100644
--- a/src/SDL.c
+++ b/src/SDL.c
@@ -186,7 +186,12 @@ const char *SDL_GetAppMetadataProperty(const char *name)
 
 
 // The initialized subsystems
-#ifdef SDL_MAIN_NEEDED
+/* Voxelium: on iOS SDL_main.h asks for SDL's own main() and app delegate
+ * (SDL_RunApp), which mark SDL ready. Here SDL is a library loaded into an
+ * app that already runs (Minecraft through LWJGL calls SDL_Init and never
+ * SDL_SetMainReady), and the UIKit driver needs neither, so it starts ready.
+ * SDL's main thread is then the first thread that calls into SDL. */
+#if defined(SDL_MAIN_NEEDED) && !defined(SDL_PLATFORM_IOS)
 static bool SDL_MainIsReady = false;
 #else
 static bool SDL_MainIsReady = true;
